{"type":"text","timestamp":1794323900149,"sessionID":"ses_e3a15e872fferShHubfyy4fOxe","part":{"id":"prt_1c609e6d8001HdZdLEDzmNPHiz","messageID":"msg_1c609c272001YcBX4LXhXW0w2k","sessionID":"ses_e3a15e872fferShHubfyy4fOxe","type":"text","text":"Done. Summary of the complete build:\n\n**Backend** (`backend/app.py`): SQLite (`./data/recipes.db`, seeded with 4 recipes/2 categories on first start), `POST /api/auth/register|login` with bearer tokens, full recipe CRUD with ordered ingredients, `q`/`category`/paging filters, `/api/categories`, `/api/health`, JSON errors (400/401/403/404/409/204), SPA frontend serving.\n\n**Frontend** (`frontend/`): React + TS + Tailwind v4 — recipe list (cards, category dropdown, title search, paging), recipe detail (ingredients as list, instructions with line breaks preserved, author-only edit/delete with hybrid confirmation), add/edit form with dynamic ingredient rows + per-field validation messages, sign-in/register, auth context with localStorage token.\n\n**Verified**: 65/65 API smoke tests, `tsc --noEmit` clean, `npm run build` clean, fresh `npm ci` + build works, multi-worker seeding safe, unicode/`%`/`_` search edge cases pass.\n\n**Fixed in this session**: `pip install -r requirements.txt -c requirements.lock` (the Dockerfile's exact command) failed because hashed constraints flip pip's `--require-hashes` mode while plain requirements lack hashes — on pip 24 and 25 alike. `backend/requirements.txt` is now the full hash-pinned closure (same pins/hashes as the untouched `requirements.lock`); both documented and standalone installs verified on both pip versions.\n\nWorkspace is clean — temp test files, logs, and `data/` removed; `docker build` flow (`npm ci` + constraints install) validated piecewise since Docker isn't available here.","time":{"start":1794323900120,"end":1794323900123}}}
